  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the implementation of EAC, this now removes key mods such as Closed Captions, Voice Falloff, Ease of Use Menus and more. For example with me having Sickle Cell, it can be hard for me to move at times from pain, so I relax in VRChat while laying down with friends or my SO to cope. However a mod I used allowed me to have the main menu on my hands, allowing me to lay down while using the menu so I don't have to strain while in pain just to use the menu. I believe that before putting in any anti cheat like EAC, the modding community should have been consulted first to get more information about \"Wholesome Modding\" so the team can start to implement these features into the game, or even whitelist these mods. And then once this is done, anti-cheat can be put in without harming the less abled people who play VRC. Some mods like:\nClosed Captions\nAnti-Crash\nVoice Falloff/Volume Falloff\nEasy Access Menus\nMenu Scaling\nBrightness/Night Mode Sliders\nAvatar Hiders\nAnd more",
